WEBVTT

NOTE Perovial Registry film v0.5. Narration captions. Scenes without narration have on-screen text only.

1
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.320
Peyronie's disease is hard to measure.

2
00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:12.750
A new treatment deserves a careful record.

3
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.540
How many courses did we start?

4
00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:26.010
How many were finished?

5
00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:27.850
Did the curve improve?

6
00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:29.800
Open one dashboard.

7
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:33.090
This is the Perovial Registry.

8
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:38.000
The Perovial Registry keeps each course of injections,

9
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.340
each assessment and each outcome in one record,

10
00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:44.950
inside the Trust's own Microsoft 365.

11
00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:48.650
Start a case with a year of birth and a date.

12
00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:51.110
No name. No hospital number.

13
00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:55.150
Each patient is known only by a Registry ID.

14
00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:58.650
Record the history and examination once.

15
00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:00.820
The phase of the disease, the deformity,

16
00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:04.550
and the suitability check from the instructions for use.

17
00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:08.560
Then, one entry for every weekly injection.

18
00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:11.120
Scan the box for the lot and expiry.

19
00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:12.410
Slide for pain.

20
00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:14.750
Save, and move on.

21
00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:17.760
The same measures are taken at baseline,

22
00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:21.760
at the end of the course, and at three, six and twelve months.

23
00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:26.750
Curvature, plaque size, pain, and how the patient feels.

24
00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:31.510
At the visit, the app prints a letter on the Trust's letterhead.

25
00:01:31.510 --> 00:01:35.100
It carries a QR code and a single-use check-in code,

26
00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:39.150
and nothing that identifies the patient.

27
00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:42.090
At home, the patient scans the code

28
00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:44.760
and answers fourteen short questions.

29
00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:47.820
It takes about three minutes.

30
00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:58.050
Every question has a published source.

31
00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:01.660
The European guideline, the hyaluronic acid studies,

32
00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:03.650
and established scales.

33
00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:07.750
They are registry items, not a new questionnaire.

34
00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:11.130
The dashboard shows the site's own outcomes,

35
00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:13.940
each with the number of cases behind it.

36
00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:18.950
Counts below five are hidden, so that no one can be picked out.

37
00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:21.750
One press saves once.

38
00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:24.120
Registry IDs never repeat.

39
00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:27.350
And a locked case stays locked.

40
00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:31.160
The app runs on the Trust's own systems.

41
00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:33.700
Collecting data is quick and convenient,

42
00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:36.400
for the team and for the patient.

43
00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:40.540
Every case adds to a prospective record that keeps on growing.

44
00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:42.180
And other centres can join,

45
00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:45.150
opening the way to multicentre studies.

46
00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:50.670
Built for the clinic, the patient, and the service.

47
00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:54.480
The Perovial Registry.

48
00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:57.340
Ready for clinical review.
